# --- Option A: Supabase (same DB as Next.js in prod / local dev)
# Run migrations in Supabase → SQL Editor (paste `migrations/001_bookings.sql`), or use psql with the
# **session** or **direct** connection string from Dashboard → Database (not required in this file for Next).
#
# For one-off local psql against Supabase, use the “Session mode” or direct (5432) URI from the dashboard.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:PASSWORD@db.PROJECT_REF.supabase.co:5432/postgres?sslmode=require

# --- Option B: Docker Postgres (offline / CI only)
# Copy to `.env`, then: `docker compose up -d` and apply `migrations/001_bookings.sql`.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://mentemaestra:mentemaestra_dev@127.0.0.1:5433/mentemaestra
